## THE WORK (ALL READ-ONLY)
1. **Clone develop at the live tip into YOUR OWN scratchpad** (never the shared checkout, never anywhere under 2_Project_Files). Use the project's own configured read access; no secret in argv. Record the full sha and the clone path in the plan and in every mail.
2. **Find the register-connector rotate path** (api-gateway and/or originate and/or shared; SEARCH, do not assume; list the terms you searched and the hit counts). Answer each, with file:line at the sha:
   a. On rotate, are the OLD key's scopes copied to the NEW key? Specifically `subjects:erase`. If not copied, what scopes does the new key get, and from where (defaults, request body, organisation, the connector's registration)?
   b. Is the 3,000-an-hour rate limit a property of the key (copied or not), of the organisation, of the scope, or global? Where is 3,000 defined (file:line)? Is it the same number on every code path, or does a second definition exist?
   c. Does the answer differ for keys minted before KS-869 (6 Sep; no connector id)? What does the rotate path do when the old key has no connector id?
   d. Any test that pins (a), (b) or (c) today: name it (file and test name). Run it ONLY if it is cheap and runs inside YOUR OWN clone with no network to any running stack, no database you do not own and no credential; otherwise say NOT RUN and why.
   e. Two plain-words sentences Kam can read: what a rotated key carries today, and what that means for dev-ps's re-key. If the code does not settle it (for example the answer depends on data in a running system), say so rather than infer.
3. **NO write anywhere** except your own scratchpad, your own REC folder (/Volumes/DevMASTER/!CODING/Secuura/Blockchain/5_Project_History/<machine date>_seatS-122nd/, from `date`) and the vault daily-note block: no Linear comment, no ticket, no PR, no push, no mail to any human, no request to any running stack (Kintsugi, demo, any live host). Reading Linear is permitted only for the KS-843 comment text itself (by python urllib raw JSON) if you need to confirm the question; never through gh output for text holding backslash-u sequences.
